lue="json">JSON strings · preserves line breaks</option></select></label><div class="row"><label>Target label (exact)<input id="label-filter" maxlength="160" placeholder="Any target label"></label><label>Protected source/group (exact)<input id="group-filter" maxlength="240" placeholder="Any stored group ID"></label></div><label>Rights note (exact)<input id="rights-filter" maxlength="2000" placeholder="Any note; enter unknown for missing notes" aria-describedby="metadata-filter-help"></label><p id="metadata-filter-help">Exact, case-sensitive values; leave blank for any. For values with line breaks, choose JSON strings and enter double-quoted values: &quot;first\nsecond&quot; for LF, \r for CR and \r\n for CRLF. Escape literal backslashes as \\ and quotes as \&quot;. Groups match IDs stored on the record, not all related sources. Rights notes are metadata, not permission decisions. Missing notes appear as unknown. Filtered results are dynamic; saved fixed membership and release selection stay separate.</p><button>Search collection</button></form><p id="analysis"></p><div class="row"><button id="select-page">Select page</button><button id="clear-selection">Clear selection</button></div><details id="saved-search-panel"><summary>Saved searches · dynamic results</summary><p>Save the entered search and filters. Open explicitly to search the current collection; new matching records can appear. Fixed selections, editor drafts and review decisions stay separate. Up to 100 searches. Search text is single-line; exact metadata values may contain line breaks.</p><form id="save-search-form"><label>Search name<input id="search-name" maxlength="120" required></label><button id="save-search">Save entered filters</button></form><label>Saved dynamic search<select id="saved-search"><option value="">Choose a saved dynamic search</option></select></label><div class="row"><button id="open-search">Open dynamic search</button><button id="cancel-search-open" hidden>Cancel opening</button><button id="refresh-searches">Refresh searches</button></div><form id="rename-search-form"><label>New search name<input id="search-rename" maxlength="120" required></label><button id="rename-search">Rename search</button></form><button id="delete-search">Delete saved search</button><p id="saved-search-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><details open id="saved-selection-panel"><summary>Saved fixed selections</summary><p>Save the chosen records at their exact revisions. Searches and filters stay separate; saving or opening never approves annotations.</p><form id="save-selection-form"><label>Selection name<input id="selection-name" maxlength="120" required></label><button id="save-selection">Save selected records as a new set</button></form><label>Saved set<select id="saved-selection"><option value="">Choose a saved selection</option></select></label><div class="row"><button id="load-selection">Open fixed selection</button><button id="cancel-selection-load" hidden>Cancel opening</button><button id="refresh-selections">Refresh saved sets</button></div><form id="rename-selection-form"><label>New name<input id="selection-rename" maxlength="120" required></label><button>Rename saved set</button></form><button id="delete-selection">Delete saved set</button><p id="saved-selection-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><ul id="saved-selection-issues"></ul></details><details open id="curation-panel"><summary>Curation diagnostics</summary><p>Inspect current metadata in all applied collection results or exact selected IDs. Selection revision pairs stay fixed. Counts describe metadata, not permission or model quality. Missing sources means deleted source records; file integrity is checked during release.</p><label>Scope<select id="curation-scope"><option value="filtered">All applied collection results</option><option value="selected">Exact selected IDs · current facts</option></select></label><label>Diagnostic<select id="curation-category"><option value="duplicates">Exact decoded-content duplicates</option><option value="unlabeled">Unlabeled · no annotation</option><option value="missing_sources">Missing source records</option><option value="unknown_rights">Unknown rights notes</option><option value="references">Stale / unavailable selected references</option></select></label><button id="curation-refresh" type="button">Refresh diagnostics</button><p id="curation-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Refresh to inspect current metadata.</p><p id="curation-counts"></p><ol id="curation-results"></ol><div class="row"><button id="curation-previous" type="button" disabled>Previous diagnostic page</button><span id="curation-page"></span><button id="curation-next" type="button" disabled>Next diagnostic page</button></div></details><div id="records"></div><div class="row"><button id="previous">Previous</button><span id="page"></span><button id="next">Next</button></div></section>
-<section class="editor"><h2>Annotate & review</h2><details id="pumas-gateway-panel"><summary>Find Pumas for annotation</summary><p>Inspect a local gateway before choosing it for a proposal. Build features describe the compiled program; they do not prove model readiness. Gateway details are advertised, without authentication of library ownership. Existing manual gateway URLs remain available.</p><button type="button" id="pumas-gateway-scan">Scan advertised gateways</button><label>Advertised gateway<select id="pumas-gateway-choice"></select></label><label>Use gateway for<select id="pumas-gateway-target"><option value="caption">Image caption proposal</option><option value="classification">Text label proposal</option><option value="rewrite">Grounded rewrite proposal</option></select></label><button type="button" id="pumas-gateway-use" disabled>Use selected gateway</button><p id="pumas-gateway-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Scan reads local advertisements. Choosing a gateway starts no model request.</p><details><summary>Advertised identity and observation hash</summary><pre id="pumas-gateway-metadata" hidden></pre></details></details><p id="empty-editor">Open a record to inspect its source and define its target.</p><form id="editor" hidden><h3 id="record-name"></h3><div id="image-frame"><img id="asset-image" alt="Selected annotation source" hidden><svg id="box-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></svg></div><pre id="asset-text" tabindex="0" hidden></pre><section id="audio-inspection" hidden><h4>Listen · mark · review</h4><p id="audio-metadata"></p><p>Original playback: all source channels. Timed annotations and interval playback use the selected source channel.</p><audio id="audio-player" controls preload="metadata" aria-label="Play original audio, all channels"></audio><a id="audio-download">Download original WAV</a><svg id="audio-waveform" viewBox="0 0 600 96" role="img" aria-label="Audio waveform"></svg><p id="audio-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="audio-empty">No intervals yet. Add a transcript or class label before review.</p><ol id="audio-segments"></ol><label>Source channel<select id="audio-channel"></select></label><div class="audio-fields"><label>Start frame (included)<input id="audio-start" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="0"></label><label>End frame (excluded)<input id="audio-end" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1"></label></div><p id="audio-time-hint"></p><div class="audio-actions"><button id="audio-play-interval" type="button">Play interval / channel</button><button id="audio-stop" type="button">Pause playback</button></div><label>Human transcript<textarea id="audio-transcript" rows="2" maxlength="4000" placeholder="What you heard in this interval"></textarea></label><div class="audio-fields"><label>Class label (optional)<input id="audio-label" maxlength="80" placeholder="e.g. impact"></label><label>Speaker (optional)<input id="audio-speaker" maxlength="120" placeholder="Human-assigned speaker"></label></div><div class="audio-actions"><button id="audio-add" type="button">Add interval</button><button id="audio-clear-fields" type="button">Clear interval fields</button></div><p>Save targets below, then explicitly mark human reviewed. One reviewed labelled interval can use the local audio classification recipe. ASR, cropping and resampling are unavailable.</p></section><section id="sequence-inspection" hidden><p>Whole accepted-state trajectory. Contract checks leave data unreviewed. Transport-only data has no qualified training consumer. Pressure describes the last accepted interval projection.</p><a id="sequence-download">Download original run.json + frames.jsonl bundle</a><details open><summary>Metadata and frame index</summary><pre id="sequence-metadata"></pre></details><label>Human review note<textarea id="sequence-note" maxlength="4000" rows="3"></textarea></label></section><section id="pointcloud-inspection" hidden><a id="pointcloud-download">Download original PLY + sidecar bundle</a><p id="pointcloud-preview-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="pointcloud-preview"></div><details><summary>Native metadata and declared provenance</summary><pre id="pointcloud-metadata"></pre></details><label>Human point cloud review note<textarea id="pointcloud-note" maxlength="4000" rows="3"></textarea></label></section><section id="scientific-inspection" hidden><a id="scientific-download">Download original scientific bundle</a><div class="scientific-controls"><label>Frame<select id="scientific-frame"></select></label><label>Field<select id="scientific-field"></select></label><label>Index axis<select id="scientific-axis"><option value="z">Z</option><option value="y">Y</option><option value="x">X</option></select></label><label>Slice index<input id="scientific-index" type="number" min="0" value="0" step="1"></label></div><p id="scientific-status" role="status"></p><canvas id="scientific-canvas" role="img" hidden></canvas><p id="scientific-coordinates"></p><div class="scientific-controls"><label>Probe row<input id="scientific-row" type="number" min="0" value="0" step="1"></label><label>Probe column<input id="scientific-column" type="number" min="0" value="0" step="1"></label></div><p id="scientific-probe" role="status"></p><details><summary>Native fields, geometry and declared provenance</summary><pre id="scientific-metadata"></pre></details><label>Whole-sequence review note<textarea id="scientific-note" maxlength="4000" rows="3"></textarea></label></section><section id="volume-inspection" hidden><a id="volume-download">Download original NPY + sidecar bundle</a><p id="volume-preview-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="volume-preview"></div><details><summary>Native metadata and declared provenance</summary><pre id="volume-metadata"></pre></details><label>Human volume review note<textarea id="volume-note" maxlength="4000" rows="3"></textarea></label></section><section id="mesh-inspection" hidden><p>Original geometry stays unchanged. Imports start as drafts; human review remains explicit. Units and frame are source declarations, not physics validation.</p><a id="mesh-download">Download original PLY + sidecar bundle</a><p id="mesh-preview-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="mesh-projections"></div><details><summary>Geometry metadata and declared provenance</summary><pre id="mesh-metadata"></pre></details><label>Human geometry review note<textarea id="mesh-note" maxlength="4000" rows="3"></textarea></label></section><label>Task<select id="task"></select></label><label id="label-control">Class / target label<input id="label" maxlength="80" value="object"></label><div id="corpus-controls" hidden><label>Corpus review note<textarea id="corpus-note" rows="4" maxlength="8000" aria-describedby="corpus-review-help"></textarea></label><p id="corpus-review-help">Review this whole document for plain-text training and leave a note (up to 4,000 Unicode code points). Explicitly choose Human reviewed when saving. Classification/entity approval does not approve corpus use. Canonical NFC/LF text stays unchanged.</p></div><div id="caption-controls" hidden><label>Accepted caption<textarea id="caption" rows="5" maxlength="8000" aria-describedby="caption-help"></textarea></label><p id="caption-help">Describe the visible image in up to 4,000 Unicode code points. Check objects, counts, colors, composition and style. A generation prompt stays in source provenance and is never copied into this caption.</p></div><p>Each record has one current task. Saving a different task replaces its current target; earlier targets remain in revision history.</p><div id="classification-help">One class label for this record.</div><div id="detection-controls" hidden><p>Drag a box on the image, or enter pixel-edge coordinates. Right and bottom edges are exclusive.</p><div class="row"><label>X<input id="box-x" type="number" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Y<input id="box-y" type="number" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Width<input id="box-width" type="number" min="1" value="10"></label><label>Height<input id="box-height" type="number" min="1" value="10"></label></div><button type="button" id="add-box">Add box</button></div><div id="entity-controls" hidden><p>Select text above, then add its span. Offsets count Unicode code points.</p><button type="button" id="add-span">Add selected span</button><div class="row"><label>Start<input id="span-start" type="number" min="0" value="0"></label><label>End<input id="span-end" type="number" min="1" value="1"></label><button type="button" id="add-offset-span">Add offsets</button></div></div><ol id="targets"></ol><label>Protected groups (one per line)<textarea id="groups" rows="2" required></textarea></label><label>Review state<select id="record-review"><option value="draft">Draft</option><option value="human_reviewed">I reviewed this annotation</option></select></label><p id="record-provenance"></p><div class="row"><button id="save">Save annotation</button><button type="button" id="reload">Discard edits / reload</button><button type="button" id="history">Revision history</button></div><pre id="history-output" hidden></pre></form><details id="caption-proposal-panel" hidden><summary>Propose a caption for this image</summary><p>Choose Pumas typed v1 for an advertised Image→Text model/profile, or use a separately compatible vision endpoint. Availability is a live observation; it does not qualify model accuracy.</p><p>One selected image, one model request. A served listing does not prove vision or JSON compatibility. Incompatible requests fail without fallback. Captions remain proposals until you explicitly apply a draft, then separately review it.</p><p>For reload recovery, this tab temporarily retains the request ID, image revisions, gateway/model, guidance and seed until the server outcome is reconciled. No image bytes or model responses are stored in the browser. Requests never replay automatically.</p><form id="caption-proposal-form"><label>Gateway API<select id="caption-proposal-protocol"><option value="legacy">Compatible API</option><option value="pumas_typed_v1">Pumas typed v1</option></select></label><label>Exact Pumas profile (optional)<input id="caption-proposal-profile" maxlength="128" placeholder="Resolve selected profile"></label><button id="caption-proposal-capabilities" type="button">Inspect selected capabilities</button><details><summary>Selected capability observation</summary><pre id="caption-proposal-capability-metadata" hidden></pre></details><label>Pumas-compatible gateway URL<input id="caption-proposal-url" type="url" value="http://127.0.0.1:8765" required></label><button id="caption-proposal-models" type="button">List served models</button><label>Model<select id="caption-proposal-model" required></select></label><label>Caption guidance<textarea id="caption-proposal-guidance" maxlength="4000" required>Describe only what is visible in this image.</textarea></label><label>Requested seed<input id="caption-proposal-seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="42" required></label><p>The original image stays local; this explicit request sends an oriented JPEG copy, at most 1600 pixels on its longest side, to the selected endpoint. Requested seeds do not guarantee model reproducibility.</p><button id="caption-proposal-submit">Request caption proposal</button></form><button id="caption-proposal-refresh" type="button">Refresh caption requests</button><p id="caption-proposal-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="caption-proposal-jobs"></div></details><details id="text-classification-proposal-panel" hidden><summary>Propose a class for this unannotated text</summary><p>One existing unannotated text, one model request. Define the exact labels first. The model must choose one offered label or explicitly abstain; unknown or malformed outputs fail without a fallback. Apply creates a draft for your separate review.</p><form id="text-classification-proposal-form"><label>Gateway API<select id="text-classification-proposal-protocol"><option value="legacy">Compatible API</option><option value="pumas_typed_v1">Pumas typed v1</option></select></label><label>Exact Pumas profile (optional)<input id="text-classification-proposal-profile" maxlength="128" placeholder="Resolve selected model profile"></label><button type="button" id="text-classification-proposal-capabilities">Inspect selected capabilities</button><p>Typed v1 sends finite requests. Text messages only; seed is unavailable. Generation runs until completion, failure or cancellation. Capability inspection has a separate bounded discovery budget.</p><pre id="text-classification-proposal-capability-metadata" hidden></pre><label>Pumas-compatible gateway URL<input id="text-classification-proposal-url" type="url" value="http://127.0.0.1:8765" required></label><button id="text-classification-proposal-models" type="button">List served text models</button><label>Model<select id="text-classification-proposal-model" required></select></label><label>Exact label choices · JSON array<textarea id="text-classification-proposal-labels" rows="4" maxlength="30000" required aria-describedby="text-classification-proposal-label-help">[]</textarea></label><p id="text-classification-proposal-label-help">Enter 1–30 unique strings, for example ["schedule", "cancel"]. Each label has 1–80 Unicode code points and no leading or trailing whitespace. JSON preserves exact internal whitespace and Unicode; no label is trimmed or guessed. Choices are frozen per request.</p><label>Classification guidance<textarea id="text-classification-proposal-guidance" rows="3" maxlength="4000" required>Choose one exact offered label only when supported by the source text; otherwise abstain.</textarea></label><label>Requested seed<input id="text-classification-proposal-seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="42" required></label><p>This explicit request sends the exact captured text, guidance and labels to the selected endpoint. Requested seeds do not guarantee reproducibility. Keep the frozen choices and request settings unchanged when applying; inspect evidence to restore them after reload.</p><button id="text-classification-proposal-submit">Request classification proposal</button></form><button id="text-classification-proposal-refresh" type="button">Refresh classification requests</button><button id="text-classification-proposal-restore" type="button">Restore pending request settings</button><button id="text-classification-proposal-open-pending" type="button">Open pending source</button><pre id="text-classification-proposal-pending-evidence" hidden></pre><p id="text-classification-proposal-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="text-classification-proposal-jobs"></div></details><details id="rights-note-panel" hidden open><summary>Correct rights note</summary><p>This note is metadata, not a permission decision. Saving changes the record revision and history; original source evidence and annotation review stay unchanged. Saved sets keep their old revisions. Reselect current records before release.</p><form id="rights-note-form"><label>Entry format<select id="rights-note-format"><option value="text">Plain text</option><option value="json">JSON string · preserves CR/LF</option></select></label><label>Current rights note<textarea id="rights-note-value" rows="4" maxlength="2000"></textarea></label><p>Up to 1,000 Unicode code points. Blank means unknown. Save or discard annotation edits first. JSON strings preserve existing carriage returns; plain text preserves line feeds.</p><div class="row"><button id="rights-note-save">Save rights note</button><button type="button" id="rights-note-cancel">Cancel note edit</button></div></form><p id="rights-note-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><details id="preferences-panel" hidden open><summary>Comparative judgments</summary><p>Choose two distinct answers to this prompt, then explicitly judge them. Answer order, model scores and answer review never decide preference. Judgment review is independent.</p><button id="preference-new" type="button">New judgment</button><button id="preference-refresh" type="button">Refresh judgments &amp; answers</button><p id="preference-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="preference-list"></div><form id="preference-form" hidden><label>Left answer<select id="preference-left" required></select></label><pre id="preference-left-text" tabindex="0"></pre><label>Right answer<select id="preference-right" required></select></label><pre id="preference-right-text" tabindex="0"></pre><label>Comparative outcome<select id="preference-outcome" required><option value="">Choose outcome explicitly</option><option value="left">Prefer left answer</option><option value="right">Prefer right answer</option><option value="tie">Tie · no chosen/rejected row</option><option value="abstain">Abstain · no chosen/rejected row</option></select></label><label>Rationale<textarea id="preference-rationale" rows="3" maxlength="8000"></textarea></label><label>Judgment review<select id="preference-review"><option value="draft">Draft judgment</option><option value="human_reviewed">I reviewed this exact comparison</option></select></label><button id="preference-save">Save judgment</button><button id="preference-cancel" type="button">Cancel judgment edit</button><button id="preference-history" type="button">Judgment history</button><button id="preference-delete" type="button" hidden>Delete judgment</button><p id="preference-editor-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form><pre id="preference-history-output" hidden></pre></details><details id="responses-panel" hidden open><summary>Instruction answers</summary><p>Author independent answers to the text above. Answers have their own revisions and review; existing classes and entity spans stay intact.</p><div class="row"><button id="response-new" type="button">Add answer</button><button id="response-refresh" type="button">Refresh answers</button></div><div id="response-list"></div><form id="response-form" hidden><label>Entry format<select id="response-entry-format"><option value="text">Plain text · LF newlines</option><option value="json">JSON string · exact CR and CRLF</option></select></label><label>Completion<textarea id="response-completion" rows="6" aria-describedby="response-help"></textarea></label><p id="response-help">Up to 200,000 Unicode code points. Spaces and Unicode are preserved. Use JSON string entry to retain carriage returns. Editing resets this answer's review to draft.</p><label>Answer review<select id="response-review"><option value="draft">Draft</option><option value="human_reviewed">I reviewed this exact answer</option></select></label><div class="row"><button id="response-save">Save answer</button><button id="response-cancel" type="button">Cancel answer edit</button><button id="response-history" type="button">Answer history</button></div><p id="response-editor-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><pre id="response-history-output" hidden></pre></form><p id="response-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details></section>
