g. Classification/entity approval does not approve corpus use. Canonical NFC/LF text stays unchanged.</p></div><div id="caption-controls" hidden><label>Accepted caption<textarea id="caption" rows="5" maxlength="8000" aria-describedby="caption-help"></textarea></label><p id="caption-help">Describe the visible image in up to 4,000 Unicode code points. Check objects, counts, colors, composition and style. A generation prompt stays in source provenance and is never copied into this caption.</p></div><p>Each record has one current task. Saving a different task replaces its current target; earlier targets remain in revision history.</p><div id="classification-help">One class label for this record.</div><div id="detection-controls" hidden><p>Drag a box on the image, or enter pixel-edge coordinates. Right and bottom edges are exclusive.</p><div class="row"><label>X<input id="box-x" type="number" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Y<input id="box-y" type="number" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Width<input id="box-width" type="number" min="1" value="10"></label><label>Height<input id="box-height" type="number" min="1" value="10"></label></div><button type="button" id="add-box">Add box</button></div><div id="entity-controls" hidden><p>Select text above, then add its span. Offsets count Unicode code points.</p><button type="button" id="add-span">Add selected span</button><div class="row"><label>Start<input id="span-start" type="number" min="0" value="0"></label><label>End<input id="span-end" type="number" min="1" value="1"></label><button type="button" id="add-offset-span">Add offsets</button></div></div><ol id="targets"></ol><label>Protected groups (one per line)<textarea id="groups" rows="2" required></textarea></label><label>Review state<select id="record-review"><option value="draft">Draft</option><option value="human_reviewed">I reviewed this annotation</option></select></label><p id="record-provenance"></p><div class="row"><button id="save">Save annotation</button><button type="button" id="reload">Discard edits / reload</button><button type="button" id="history">Revision history</button></div><pre id="history-output" hidden></pre></form><details id="caption-proposal-panel" hidden><summary>Propose a caption for this image</summary><p>Choose Pumas typed v1 for an advertised Image→Text model/profile, or use a separately compatible vision endpoint. Availability is a live observation; it does not qualify model accuracy.</p><p>One selected image, one model request. A served listing does not prove vision or JSON compatibility. Incompatible requests fail without fallback. Captions remain proposals until you explicitly apply a draft, then separately review it.</p><p>For reload recovery, this tab temporarily retains the request ID, image revisions, gateway/model, guidance and seed until the server outcome is reconciled. No image bytes or model responses are stored in the browser. Requests never replay automatically.</p><form id="caption-proposal-form"><label>Gateway API<select id="caption-proposal-protocol"><option value="legacy">Compatible API</option><option value="pumas_typed_v1">Pumas typed v1</option></select></label><label>Exact Pumas profile (optional)<input id="caption-proposal-profile" maxlength="128" placeholder="Resolve selected profile"></label><button id="caption-proposal-capabilities" type="button">Inspect selected capabilities</button><details><summary>Selected capability observation</summary><pre id="caption-proposal-capability-metadata" hidden></pre></details><label>Pumas-compatible gateway URL<input id="caption-proposal-url" type="url" value="http://127.0.0.1:8765" required></label><button id="caption-proposal-models" type="button">List served models</button><label>Model<select id="caption-proposal-model" required></select></label><label>Caption guidance<textarea id="caption-proposal-guidance" maxlength="4000" required>Describe only what is visible in this image.</textarea></label><label>Requested seed<input id="caption-proposal-seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="42" required></label><p>The original image stays local; this explicit request sends an oriented JPEG copy, at most 1600 pixels on its longest side, to the selected endpoint. Requested seeds do not guarantee model reproducibility.</p><button id="caption-proposal-submit">Request caption proposal</button></form><button id="caption-proposal-refresh" type="button">Refresh caption requests</button><p id="caption-proposal-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="caption-proposal-jobs"></div></details><details id="text-classification-proposal-panel" hidden><summary>Propose a class for this unannotated text</summary><p>One existing unannotated text, one model request. Define the exact labels first. The model must choose one offered label or explicitly abstain; unknown or malformed outputs fail without a fallback. Apply creates a draft for your separate review.</p><form id="text-classification-proposal-form"><label>Gateway API<select id="text-classification-proposal-protocol"><option value="legacy">Compatible API</option><option value="pumas_typed_v1">Pumas typed v1</option></select></label><label>Exact Pumas profile (optional)<input id="text-classification-proposal-profile" maxlength="128" placeholder="Resolve selected model profile"></label><button type="button" id="text-classification-proposal-capabilities">Inspect selected capabilities</button><p>Typed v1 sends finite requests. Text messages only; seed is unavailable. Generation runs until completion, failure or cancellation. Capability inspection has a separate bounded discovery budget.</p><pre id="text-classification-proposal-capability-metadata" hidden></pre><label>Pumas-compatible gateway URL<input id="text-classification-proposal-url" type="url" value="http://127.0.0.1:8765" required></label><button id="text-classification-proposal-models" type="button">List served text models</button><label>Model<select id="text-classification-proposal-model" required></select></label><label>Exact label choices · JSON array<textarea id="text-classification-proposal-labels" rows="4" maxlength="30000" required aria-describedby="text-classification-proposal-label-help">[]</textarea></label><p id="text-classification-proposal-label-help">Enter 1–30 unique strings, for example ["schedule", "cancel"]. Each label has 1–80 Unicode code points and no leading or trailing whitespace. JSON preserves exact internal whitespace and Unicode; no label is trimmed or guessed. Choices are frozen per request.</p><label>Classification guidance<textarea id="text-classification-proposal-guidance" rows="3" maxlength="4000" required>Choose one exact offered label only when supported by the source text; otherwise abstain.</textarea></label><label>Requested seed<input id="text-classification-proposal-seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="42" required></label><p>This explicit request sends the exact captured text, guidance and labels to the selected endpoint. Requested seeds do not guarantee reproducibility. Keep the frozen choices and request settings unchanged when applying; inspect evidence to restore them after reload.</p><button id="text-classification-proposal-submit">Request classification proposal</button></form><button id="text-classification-proposal-refresh" type="button">Refresh classification requests</button><button id="text-classification-proposal-restore" type="button">Restore pending request settings</button><button id="text-classification-proposal-open-pending" type="button">Open pending source</button><pre id="text-classification-proposal-pending-evidence" hidden></pre><p id="text-classification-proposal-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="text-classification-proposal-jobs"></div></details><details id="rights-note-panel" hidden open><summary>Correct rights note</summary><p>This note is metadata, not a permission decision. Saving changes the record revision and history; original source evidence and annotation review stay unchanged. Saved sets keep their old revisions. Reselect current records before release.</p><form id="rights-note-form"><label>Entry format<select id="rights-note-format"><option value="text">Plain text</option><option value="json">JSON string · preserves CR/LF</option></select></label><label>Current rights note<textarea id="rights-note-value" rows="4" maxlength="2000"></textarea></label><p>Up to 1,000 Unicode code points. Blank means unknown. Save or discard annotation edits first. JSON strings preserve existing carriage returns; plain text preserves line feeds.</p><div class="row"><button id="rights-note-save">Save rights note</button><button type="button" id="rights-note-cancel">Cancel note edit</button></div></form><p id="rights-note-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><details id="preferences-panel" hidden open><summary>Comparative judgments</summary><p>Choose two distinct answers to this prompt, then explicitly judge them. Answer order, model scores and answer review never decide preference. Judgment review is independent.</p><button id="preference-new" type="button">New judgment</button><button id="preference-refresh" type="button">Refresh judgments &amp; answers</button><p id="preference-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="preference-list"></div><form id="preference-form" hidden><label>Left answer<select id="preference-left" required></select></label><pre id="preference-left-text" tabindex="0"></pre><label>Right answer<select id="preference-right" required></select></label><pre id="preference-right-text" tabindex="0"></pre><label>Comparative outcome<select id="preference-outcome" required><option value="">Choose outcome explicitly</option><option value="left">Prefer left answer</option><option value="right">Prefer right answer</option><option value="tie">Tie · no chosen/rejected row</option><option value="abstain">Abstain · no chosen/rejected row</option></select></label><label>Rationale<textarea id="preference-rationale" rows="3" maxlength="8000"></textarea></label><label>Judgment review<select id="preference-review"><option value="draft">Draft judgment</option><option value="human_reviewed">I reviewed this exact comparison</option></select></label><button id="preference-save">Save judgment</button><button id="preference-cancel" type="button">Cancel judgment edit</button><button id="preference-history" type="button">Judgment history</button><button id="preference-delete" type="button" hidden>Delete judgment</button><p id="preference-editor-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form><pre id="preference-history-output" hidden></pre></details><details id="responses-panel" hidden open><summary>Instruction answers</summary><p>Author independent answers to the text above. Answers have their own revisions and review; existing classes and entity spans stay intact.</p><div class="row"><button id="response-new" type="button">Add answer</button><button id="response-refresh" type="button">Refresh answers</button></div><div id="response-list"></div><form id="response-form" hidden><label>Entry format<select id="response-entry-format"><option value="text">Plain text · LF newlines</option><option value="json">JSON string · exact CR and CRLF</option></select></label><label>Completion<textarea id="response-completion" rows="6" aria-describedby="response-help"></textarea></label><p id="response-help">Up to 200,000 Unicode code points. Spaces and Unicode are preserved. Use JSON string entry to retain carriage returns. Editing resets this answer's review to draft.</p><label>Answer review<select id="response-review"><option value="draft">Draft</option><option value="human_reviewed">I reviewed this exact answer</option></select></label><div class="row"><button id="response-save">Save answer</button><button id="response-cancel" type="button">Cancel answer edit</button><button id="response-history" type="button">Answer history</button></div><p id="response-editor-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><pre id="response-history-output" hidden></pre></form><p id="response-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></details></section>
 <aside><details id="audio-import-panel"><summary>Import WAV audio</summary><p>Original PCM signed 16-bit WAV, mono or stereo, 8–96 kHz. Up to 8 MiB and 120 seconds. No inferred transcript or training.</p><form id="audio-import-form"><label>Original WAV<input id="audio-file" type="file" accept=".wav,audio/wav" required></label><label>Protected recording/session group<input id="audio-group" maxlength="120" placeholder="same-session-01"></label><label>Rights / permission note<input id="audio-rights" value="unknown" maxlength="1000"></label><button>Import original WAV</button><p id="audio-import-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></details><details open><summary>Import real assets</summary><form id="import-form"><label>Name<input id="import-name" value="Text record"></label><label>Protected source/group<input id="import-group" required placeholder="document-01 or shoot-01"></label><label>Rights / permission note<input id="rights" value="unknown"></label><label>Text<textarea id="import-text" rows="4" placeholder="Paste a text record, or choose an image below"></textarea></label><label>Image<input id="import-image" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"></label><button>Import record</button></form></details><details open id="bulk-panel"><summary>Import a real corpus</summary><form id="bulk-form"><p>Choose a UTF-8 JSONL manifest and its referenced images. Each row creates one raw draft asset; annotate and review afterward.</p><label>Manifest<input id="bulk-manifest" type="file" accept=".jsonl,application/x-ndjson" required></label><label>Referenced images<input id="bulk-images" type="file" multiple accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"></label><p>Up to 1,000 physical lines and 8 MiB per manifest. Image references must match exactly one selected filename; directories and URLs are not accepted.</p><details><summary>Row examples</summary><pre>{"kind":"text","name":"Note","text":"A real note","groups":["document-01"],"rights":"Authored"}
 {"kind":"image","file":"photo.png","groups":["shoot-01"],"rights":"Permission granted"}</pre><p>Optional name, parents and rights use the existing record fields. Supplied annotations, review states and provenance are rejected. Parents must be existing record IDs.</p></details><div class="row"><button id="bulk-start">Import rows</button><button id="bulk-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop after current row</button></div></form><p id="bulk-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to import raw assets.</p><p>Valid rows stay imported when another row fails. Stop prevents the next admission; an in-flight row may finish. Duplicates are rejected without updating existing records.</p><ol id="bulk-results"></ol><button id="bulk-check" type="button" disabled>Check pending row</button><button id="bulk-dismiss" type="button" disabled>Dismiss pending check</button></details><details id="pointcloud-import-panel"><summary>Import point cloud</summary><form id="pointcloud-import-form"><label>points.ply (2 MiB)<input id="pointcloud-file" type="file" required></label><label>points.json (32 KiB)<input id="pointcloud-manifest" type="file" accept=".json" required></label><label>Name<input id="pointcloud-name" value="Local point cloud" maxlength="200" required></label><label>Rights / permission note<input id="pointcloud-rights" value="unknown" maxlength="1000"></label><button>Validate &amp; import whole point cloud</button><p id="pointcloud-import-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></details><details id="volume-import-panel"><summary>Import volume</summary><form id="volume-import-form"><label>volume.npy (2 MiB + header)<input id="volume-file" type="file" required></label><label>volume.json (32 KiB)<input id="volume-manifest" type="file" accept=".json" required></label><label>Name<input id="volume-name" value="Local volume" maxlength="200" required></label><label>Rights / permission note<input id="volume-rights" value="unknown" maxlength="1000"></label><button>Validate &amp; import whole volume</button><p id="volume-import-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></details><details id="mesh-import-panel"><summary>Import static triangle mesh</summary><p>Select mesh.ply (ASCII PLY 1.0 triangles, xyz and optional normals) and its mesh.json sidecar declaring units, coordinate frame and provenance. Raw files stay unchanged; whole geometry families stay together. 20,000 vertices / 40,000 triangles maximum.</p><form id="mesh-import-form"><label>mesh.ply (2 MiB)<input id="mesh-ply" type="file" accept=".ply" required></label><label>mesh.json (32 KiB)<input id="mesh-manifest" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" required></label><label>Name<input id="mesh-name" value="Static triangle mesh" maxlength="200" required></label><label>Additional protected source/group (optional)<input id="mesh-group" maxlength="120"></label><label>Rights / permission note<input id="mesh-rights" value="unknown" maxlength="1000"></label><button>Validate &amp; import whole mesh</button><p id="mesh-import-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></details><details id="sequence-import-panel"><summary>Import Rheon simulation sequence</summary><p>Select the complete run.json and frames.jsonl from Rheon draft PR 20's pinned transport fixture. One 16×8×4 trajectory, constructor plus eight accepted steps. Named MAC fields stay intact. Whole trajectory and initial family stay together in splits.</p><form id="sequence-import-form"><label>run.json (64 KiB)<input id="sequence-run" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" required></label><label>frames.jsonl (2 MiB)<input id="sequence-frames" type="file" accept=".jsonl" required></label><label>Name<input id="sequence-name" value="Rheon transport sequence" maxlength="200" required></label><label>Additional protected source/group (optional)<input id="sequence-group" maxlength="120"></label><label>Rights / permission note<input id="sequence-rights" value="unknown" maxlength="1000"></label><button id="sequence-import-start">Validate & import whole trajectory</button><p id="sequence-import-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></details><details id="sequence-batch-panel"><summary>Import a folder of Rheon trajectories</summary><p>Select a folder containing only one subfolder per trajectory, each with run.json and frames.jsonl. Up to 32 complete pairs and 40 MiB of selected raw files. Each uses the pinned fee7b4a transport contract: 16×8×4, constructor plus eight accepted steps.</p><form id="sequence-batch-form"><label>Trajectory folder<input id="sequence-batch-folder" type="file" webkitdirectory multiple required></label><label>Shared protected group (optional; keeps all imported runs together)<input id="sequence-batch-group" maxlength="120"></label><label>Rights / permission note<input id="sequence-batch-rights" value="unknown" maxlength="1000"></label><div class="row"><button id="sequence-batch-start">Import whole trajectories</button><button id="sequence-batch-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop before next trajectory</button></div></form><p id="sequence-batch-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to import complete trajectories.</p><p>Successful items remain imported as drafts. An in-flight item may complete after Stop or departure. Unknown responses pause without replay. Progress is held in this page; after reload, inspect the collection. Saved-result confirmation proves admission only; source integrity and human review are separate. This is transport import, not qualified simulation training data.</p><ol id="sequence-batch-results"></ol><div class="row"><button id="sequence-batch-check" type="button" disabled>Check pending trajectory</button><button id="sequence-batch-dismiss" type="button" disabled>Dismiss pending check</button></div></details><details id="native-detection-import-panel"><summary>Import native detection release</summary><p>Choose a detection-only canonical_v1 ZIP with 1–100 images (8 MiB). Oriented PNGs and boxes become new drafts requiring your review; rights start unknown. Exported partitions and declared family links are retained. The archive omits upstream originals and unselected family members.</p><form id="native-detection-form"><label>Native detection ZIP<input id="native-detection-archive" type="file" accept=".zip,application/zip" required></label><div class="row"><button id="native-detection-start">Import detection drafts</button><button id="native-detection-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop before next record</button></div></form><p id="native-detection-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to import native detection records.</p><p>Successful records remain imported. In-flight work may complete after Stop or departure. Uncertain responses pause without replay; progress stays in this page. After reload, inspect the collection.</p><ul id="native-detection-results"></ul><div class="row"><button id="native-detection-check" disabled>Check uncertain saved result</button><button id="native-detection-dismiss" disabled>Dismiss pending check</button></div></details><details id="native-text-import-panel"><summary>Import native text-classification release</summary><p>Choose a frozen canonical_v1 ZIP. Imports its exported text and labels as new drafts. Exported text becomes the new source input; upstream original text cannot be recovered. Historical review, rights and splits grant no local approval or permission.</p><form id="native-text-form"><label>Native release ZIP<input id="native-text-archive" type="file" accept=".zip,application/zip" required></label><div class="row"><button id="native-text-start">Import classification drafts</button><button id="native-text-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop before next record</button></div></form><p id="native-text-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="row"><button id="native-text-check" disabled>Check uncertain saved result</button><button id="native-text-dismiss" disabled>Dismiss pending check</button></div><ul id="native-text-results"></ul></details>
-<details open id="caption-import-panel"><summary>Import a frozen caption corpus</summary><form id="caption-form"><p>Choose an expanded Tuldok image-caption v1 release folder with manifest.json and train/val/test metadata and PNGs.</p><label>Caption release folder<input id="caption-folder" type="file" webkitdirectory multiple required></label><p>Captions become drafts for your review. Existing split assignments and protected families are retained. Source identity is recorded as origin evidence; existing records are never updated.</p><div class="row"><button id="caption-start">Import draft captions</button><button id="caption-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop after current row</button></div></form><p id="caption-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to import native caption records.</p><ol id="caption-results"></ol><button id="caption-check" type="button" disabled>Check pending caption</button><button id="caption-dismiss" type="button" disabled>Dismiss pending check</button><p>Successful rows remain imported. Stop prevents the next admission. Batch progress stays in this page; inspect the collection after reload.</p></details><details open><summary>Generate offline</summary><form id="generate-form"><label>Recipe<select id="recipe"><option value="rectangles-v1">Rectangle detection scenes</option><option value="intent-requests-v1">Scheduling intent requests</option></select></label><div class="row"><label>Seed<input id="seed" type="number" value="42" min="0" max="4294967295"></label><label>Count<input id="count" type="number" value="12" min="1" max="100"></label></div><p>Known targets from authored scene or template state. These recipes demonstrate reproducible production; they do not establish real-world model quality. Pumas image generation remains in the corner studio.</p><button>Generate candidates</button></form></details><details open><summary>Grounded model candidates</summary><form id="grounded-form"><label>Gateway API<select id="grounded-protocol"><option value="legacy">Compatible API</option><option value="pumas_typed_v1">Pumas typed v1</option></select></label><label>Exact Pumas profile (optional)<input id="grounded-profile" maxlength="128" placeholder="Resolve selected model profile"></label><button type="button" id="grounded-capabilities">Inspect selected capabilities</button><p>Typed v1 sends finite requests. Text messages only; seed is unavailable. Generation runs until completion, failure or cancellation. Capability inspection has a separate bounded discovery budget.</p><pre id="grounded-capability-metadata" hidden></pre><p>Open a human-reviewed text-classification source. Generate class-preserving rewrite proposals using your Pumas gateway; the captured source text is sent to the selected server.</p><label>Pumas gateway URL<input id="grounded-url" type="url" value="http://127.0.0.1:8080" required></label><button type="button" id="grounded-models">Refresh served models</button><label>Served text model<select id="grounded-model" required><option value="">Refresh models first</option></select></label><label>Variation instruction<textarea id="grounded-instruction" rows="3" maxlength="2000" required>Rewrite clearly for varied phrasing while preserving every fact, intent and class.</textarea></label><div class="row"><label>Count<input id="grounded-count" type="number" min="1" max="10" value="3"></label><label>Seed<input id="grounded-seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="42"></label></div><button>Generate grounded proposals</button></form><p>Schema and exact source quotes are checked; semantic correctness is not. Admitting a candidate creates a draft that still needs annotation review before export. Requested seeds do not guarantee reproducibility across models.</p><button id="grounded-refresh">Refresh proposal requests</button><div id="grounded-jobs" aria-live="polite"></div></details><details open><summary>Freeze selected release</summary><form id="release-form"><label>Export format<select id="release-format"><option value="canonical_v1">Canonical mixed-task release</option><option value="image_caption_v1">Image captions · train/val/test</option><option value="text_classification_v1">Text classification · local TF-IDF / Naive Bayes</option><option value="audio_classification_v1">Audio classification · local features / logistic regression</option><option value="image_classification_v1">Image classes · Chapter 8 trainer</option><option value="text_corpus_v1">Text corpus · Chapter 11 byte transformer</option></select></label><p id="caption-export-help" hidden>Choose only human-reviewed image-caption records. All three splits must be nonempty. PNGs and metadata.jsonl use the pinned chapter-26 imagefolder contract; validation is exported as val. Exact pixel duplicates are rejected. Images below 512 pixels produce warnings.</p><p id="classification-export-help" hidden>For the pinned Chapter 8 image classifier (Torch 2.8 / torchvision 0.23). Select human-reviewed single-class images. The trainer needs at least two classes and each class in train, validation and test. Safe opaque folders preserve exact labels through the manifest mapping. Related sources and pixel repeats stay in one split; repeats are retained with a warning. Review class coverage below before freezing.</p><p id="corpus-export-help" hidden>Choose human-reviewed text corpus records with review notes. Exports train.txt, validation.txt and test.txt as canonical UTF-8, ordered by record ID, adding exactly two LF bytes after every document including the last; existing trailing newlines remain. All three connected-family splits must be nonempty. Reference context 128 needs train &gt;128 bytes; validation/test need ≥2 bytes. Allocation counts documents, not bytes. The 256-value raw-byte reader uses shifted windows that can cross document and UTF-8 character boundaries. Separators are not EOS or attention resets. Review byte/document/family counts below. Maximum 5,000 records and 40 MiB for the complete 